          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
            On 60 measurable held-out stems scored once against Mount Auburn's institutional botanical records, CUTMAP achieved a <strong class="text-white">median absolute error of 5.37 cm</strong> (mean bias +2.45 cm; overall RMSE 11.38 cm across all 60 stems, or <strong class="text-white">6.79 cm RMSE</strong> excluding three extreme co-dominant/flared ornamental specimens that accounted for 66% of the squared error).
          </p>
